@startuml
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam backgroundColor #fcfcfd
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam arrowColor #0f172a
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #fff7d6
skinparam noteBorderColor #b45309
skinparam noteFontColor #334155
skinparam roundcorner 16
title Activity - jms/JmsPlugin
skinparam activity {
  backgroundColor #f8fafc
  borderColor #0f172a
  fontColor #0f172a
  diamondBackgroundColor #e2e8f0
  diamondBorderColor #1d4ed8
  diamondFontColor #0f172a
  startColor #1d4ed8
  endColor #0f172a
  barColor #1d4ed8
}
start
partition "Observe and Bind" {
:Start from shared flow\nshared/diagrams/shared-reconcile-activity.svg;
:Read desired JmsPlugin spec, tracked status,\nand delete intent;
if ("Tracked or explicit OCI identity present?") then (yes)
:Get the current OCI resource via GetJmsPlugin;
else (no)
:Resolve an existing OCI resource through\nListJmsPlugin using filters compartmentId,\nagentId, id;
:Create the OCI resource via CreateJmsPlugin\nwhen no reusable match is found;
:Persist the resolved or created OCI identity\ninto status;
endif
}
if ("Delete requested?") then (yes)
partition "Delete" {
:Delete path uses DeleteJmsPlugin with required\nvia GetJmsPlugin or ListJmsPlugin to DELETED,\nNOT_FOUND confirmation;
:Confirm deletion via GetJmsPlugin or\nListJmsPlugin until OCI reaches DELETED,\nNOT_FOUND;
if ("Delete cleanup and finalizer release succeed?") then (yes)
:Remove the finalizer after delete completion;
else (no)
:Stay blocked until cleanup or finalizer\nrelease succeeds;
endif
}
stop
else (no)
partition "Lifecycle Classification" {
if ("OCI state is outside success targets?") then (yes)
:Return an unsuccessful reconcile result until\nOCI reaches ACTIVE, INACTIVE;
stop
endif
}
partition "Ready and Drift Handling" {
:Compare live OCI state against the\nrepo-authored mutation surface;
if ("Force-new or conflicting drift detected?") then (yes)
:Reject drift before OCI mutation for force-new\nfields agentId, agentType, compartmentId;
stop
endif
if ("Supported mutable drift detected?") then (yes)
:Apply UpdateJmsPlugin only for mutable fields\ndefinedTags, fleetId, freeformTags;
else (no)
:Skip the no-op mutation path;
endif
:Run provider helper hooks\ncreate=tfresource.CreateResource;\nupdate=tfresource.UpdateResource;\ndelete=tfresource.DeleteResource when the\nmatching field-driven path executes;
:Apply explicit follow-up semantics\ncreate=read-after-write;\nupdate=read-after-write; delete=confirm-delete;
:Return success for the ACTIVE, INACTIVE\nsuccess state;
:Project required status and finalizer policy\nretain-until-confirmed-delete;
:Requeue on terminating;
}
endif
stop
note right
shared diagram:
shared/diagrams/shared-reconcile-activity.svg
Start from the shared reconcile activity and
specialize provider-backed CRUD, wait, and
status-projection details here.
Controller-local activity diagrams add
list-lookup hints, secret policies, delete
handling, and open formal gaps.
archetype batch: Generated service-manager
controllers specialize the shared reconcile path
with formal runtime ownership.
service: jms
slug: jmsplugin
kind: JmsPlugin
archetype: generated-service-manager
status/finalizer: required /
retain-until-confirmed-delete
requeue: terminating
provider states: create none; update none;
delete none
follow-up: create=read-after-write;
update=read-after-write; delete=confirm-delete
supported drift: definedTags, fleetId,
freeformTags
reject before mutate: force-new fields agentId,
agentType, compartmentId
create-only fields: none
list lookup: oci_jms_jms_plugins filters
compartmentId, agentId, id; exact compartmentId
plus agentId unique match in ACTIVE or INACTIVE;
paginated list rereads are exhausted before
concluding absent; duplicate matches fail
conflicts: none
open gaps: none
JmsPlugin create and update are synchronous
reread flows. OCI returns the resource body
directly, and fleet-less registration settles in
INACTIVE rather than a provisioning bucket.
ACTIVE and INACTIVE are the only published
steady success states. NEEDS_ATTENTION stays
outside the success set, and DELETED is only a
delete-confirmation target.
Pre-create reuse scopes by exact compartmentId
plus agentId and exhausts paginated
ListJmsPlugins responses before concluding
absent. Only ACTIVE and INACTIVE summaries are
reusable.
Mutable drift is limited to fleetId,
freeformTags, and definedTags. agentId,
agentType, and compartmentId remain
replacement-only. Fleet detachment stays out of
scope because the published spec cannot
distinguish omission from clear.
Delete keeps the finalizer until rereads return
DELETED or NotFound.
end note
@enduml
